From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: the screen saver for local accounts, a slideshow
 of the Pictures folder

Settings > Wallpaper & style > Screen saver said "not available on your
device" to every local account: ChromeOS allows its screen saver for
Gmail-type Google accounts only, and fills it from Google's servers
(Google Photos, the Art gallery, the weather) or Google's own files (the
Feel the Breeze and Float on By animations, whose stand-in in Chromium
stops the session, and the Time of Day videos from a DLC that isn't
public). NickelOS's screen saver for a local account is a slideshow of the
user's own pictures, the ones in My files > Pictures and the folders in it,
with the time, made from ChromeOS's own parts:

- AmbientClientImpl allows it for a NickelOS local account (no Gaia, email
  domain or primary account checks), asks no token for one, and names its
  Pictures folder (AmbientClient::GetNickelPicturesFolder).
- AmbientController shows that folder with the slideshow ChromeOS has for
  an administrator's screen saver (AmbientManagedSlideshowUiLauncher and
  its photo controller, which read pictures from disk), whatever theme the
  prefs name, also when the screen dims (not on the lock screen only).
  ScreensaverImagesPolicyHandler::CreateForFolder lists the pictures (as
  Files shows them: no hidden files, no links followed; up to 500, a random
  choice of more) each time the screen saver starts, for the next one, and
  every minute while there are fewer than the 2 a slideshow needs.
- NickelAmbientBackendController stands in for Google's servers in place
  of the test stand-in Chromium builds have, which never answered the
  Settings page and handed out made-up addresses: the settings live for the
  session, and there are no albums, previews, weather or server addresses.
- The Settings page offers the Slideshow theme only, shows "Pictures
  folder" as the image source (no Google Photos or Art gallery, no weather
  unit), needs no network, and its previews show the Slideshow theme's
  picture with "Pictures folder: Your own pictures".

Google accounts keep ChromeOS's screen saver as it was.

